== name new_/fib/::__^1,add
name	new_fib
Ann	2
Bob	2
== name /fib/_new::__^1,add
name	fib_new
Ann	2
Bob	2
== name fib/_new::__^1,add
name	fib_new
Ann	2
Bob	2
== name new_/fib/_x::__^1,add
name	new_fib_x
Ann	2
Bob	2
== name new_/+fib.*/::__^1,add
name	new_fib	new_fib2
Ann	2	1
Bob	2	2
== name x/fib:sq/::__^1,add
name	xfib	xsq
Ann	2	2
Bob	2	5
== name new_//fib//::__^1,add
name	fib	new_fib
Ann	1	2
Bob	1	2
== name //fib//_new::__^1,add
name	fib	fib_new
Ann	1	2
Bob	1	2
== name x//fib:sq//::__^1,add
name	fib	xfib	sq	xsq
Ann	1	2	1	2
Bob	1	2	4	5
== -i name /fib/::__^1,add
name	fib
Ann	2
Bob	2
== name f/+fi.*/::__^1,add x/fib2/::__
name	ffib	ffib2	xfib2
Ann	2	1	0
Bob	2	2	1
== name a%2Fb/fib/::__
name	a/bfib
Ann	1
Bob	1
== name fib/:x::^1
pluk: the suffix [:x] of fib/:x looks like a column specification; did you want fib/:x/?
name	fib:x
Ann	1
Bob	1
== -A p//fib//::__^1,add
name	fib	fib2	sq	fx	ud	ms	num1	num2	num4	foo11	abc	dna	pfib
Ann	1	0	1	dog	1	0.142857	1	2	1	a_n_n	a	ACGTTGCA	2
Bob	1	1	4	cat	-2	0.285714	2	3	2	b_o_b	bc	CCGGTTAA	2
== -x fib p//fib//::__^1,add
name	fib2	sq	fx	ud	ms	num1	num2	num4	foo11	abc	dna	pfib
Ann	0	1	dog	1	0.142857	1	2	1	a_n_n	a	ACGTTGCA	2
Bob	1	4	cat	-2	0.285714	2	3	2	b_o_b	bc	CCGGTTAA	2
== -A2 p/fib:sq/::__^10,mul
name	fib	pfib	psq	fib2	sq	fx	ud	ms	num1	num2	num4	foo11	abc	dna
Ann	1	10	10	0	1	dog	1	0.142857	1	2	1	a_n_n	a	ACGTTGCA
Bob	1	10	40	1	4	cat	-2	0.285714	2	3	2	b_o_b	bc	CCGGTTAA
== name /fib/::__^1,add
pluk: [/fib/::__^1,add]: name [fib] already exists (use -i for in-place change)
exit 1
== name //fib//::__^1,add
pluk: [//fib//::__^1,add]: the original and the new column would both be [fib]
exit 1
== name /fib/2::^1
pluk: [/fib/2::^1]: the new name [fib2] (from column [fib]) exists already
exit 1
== name p/fib//s::^1
pluk: [p/fib//s::^1]: mixed '/' and '//' in NAME: P/SPEC/S, or P//SPEC//S to keep the original (pick's P/SPEC//S)
exit 1
== name fib//s::^1
pluk: [fib//s::^1]: SPEC//S: the keep-original form is P//SPEC//S (P may be empty: //SPEC//S)
exit 1
== name a/b/c/d::^1
pluk: [a/b/c/d::^1]: too many '/' delimiters in NAME: SPEC/S, P/SPEC/S or P//SPEC//S (a literal / is written %2F)
exit 1
== name p///fib::^1
pluk: [p///fib::^1]: '///' in NAME (a literal / is written %2F)
exit 1
== name //s::^1
pluk: [//s::^1]: SPEC//S: the keep-original form is P//SPEC//S (P may be empty: //SPEC//S)
exit 1
== name p//fib//s:=^1
pluk: [p//fib//s:=^1]: P//SPEC//S outputs the original columns; it needs '::', not ':='
exit 1
== name /nosuch/x::^1
pluk: (Compute) handle [nosuch] in compute /nosuch/x does not reference a known entity among name,fib,fib2,sq,fx,ud,ms,num1,num2,num4,foo11,abc,dna
exit 1
compute map p//2:3//s (output)
  rename prefix [p] suffix [s] keep
  column [__]
  const [1]
  op add
compute map x/+.*/ (output)
  rename prefix [x] suffix []
  const [1]
